                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we know that the patient has a large simple cyst on the right ovary, which is likely causing her pain. \n\nNext, we see that there is detectable flow in the right ovarian artery but no flow in the right ovarian vein. This suggests that there may be a problem with venous drainage from the ovary. \n\nThe ligament that is most likely to be involved in this scenario is the infundibulopelvic ligament, also known as the suspensory ligament of the ovary. This ligament contains the ovarian artery and vein, as well as nerves and lymphatics. If there is a problem with venous drainage from the ovary, it could be due to compression or torsion of the ovarian vein within this ligament. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E) Infundibulopelvic ligament.",
