                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The first thing that happens when a baby is born is that the umbilical cord is clamped and cut, and the baby is no longer receiving oxygenated blood from the placenta. The baby's lungs then have to start working on their own to oxygenate the blood.\n\nThe most likely cause of this infant's cyanosis is that the baby's lungs are not yet fully developed and are not able to oxygenate the blood properly. The inhaled medication that the baby is on (which increases smooth muscle cGMP) is likely helping to improve the baby's oxygenation status, but the baby is still not getting enough oxygen.",
