                        "cot": "The newborn boy was evaluated for tachypnea six hours after birth. He was delivered at 41 weeks' gestation via Caesarian section and the amniotic fluid was meconium-stained. His respiratory rate is 75/min, and physical examination shows increased work of breathing. X-rays of the abdomen and chest show no abnormalities. Echocardiography shows elevated pulmonary artery pressure. He is started on an inhaled medication that increases smooth muscle cGMP, and there is immediate improvement in his tachypnea and oxygenation status. Three hours later, the newborn is tachypneic and there is blue-grey discoloration of the lips, fingers, and toes. \n\nThe most likely cause of this infant's cyanosis is closure of the ductus arteriosus. The elevated pulmonary artery pressure seen on echocardiography suggests that the newborn has persistent pulmonary hypertension of the newborn (PPHN), which is a condition characterized by elevated pulmonary vascular resistance and right-to-left shunting of blood through the ductus arteriosus. The inhaled medication that increases smooth muscle cGMP likely improved the newborn's oxygenation status by dilating the pulmonary vasculature and reducing pulmonary vascular resistance. However, three hours later, the ductus arteriosus may have closed, leading to increased right-to-left shunting of blood and worsening cyanosis. \n\nOption A, increase in concentration of serum myoglobin, is not a likely cause of cyanosis in this case. Option C, oxidization of Fe2+ to Fe3+, and option D, inhibition of mitochondrial cytochrome c oxidase, are not likely causes of cyanosis in this case as they are not related to the pathophysiology of PPHN. Option E, allosteric alteration of heme groups, is also not a likely cause of cyanosis in this case.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0eaf0182-a349-4d20-bea4-5c9a794243b0",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Closure of the ductus arteriosus.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
