                        "id": "94f9309a-ec85-47dc-a049-2bdd94f3577a",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Meconium-stained amniotic fluid can lead to meconium aspiration syndrome, which can cause respiratory distress in newborns. Elevated pulmonary artery pressure can indicate pulmonary hypertension, which can also cause respiratory distress and cyanosis. Inhaled medications that increase smooth muscle cGMP can help alleviate pulmonary hypertension.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of cyanosis?\n2. What causes blue-grey discoloration of the lips, fingers, and toes?\n3. What is the ductus arteriosus and what is its function?\n4. What is Fe2+ and Fe3+ and how are they related to cyanosis?\n5. What is mitochondrial cytochrome c oxidase and how is it related to cyanosis?\n6. What are heme groups and how are they related to cyanosis?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Cyanosis is a bluish discoloration of the skin and mucous membranes caused by an increase in the concentration of reduced hemoglobin in the blood.\n2. Blue-grey discoloration of the lips, fingers, and toes is a symptom of cyanosis.\n3. The ductus arteriosus is a blood vessel that connects the pulmonary artery to the aorta in a fetus. Its function is to bypass the non-functioning lungs and deliver oxygenated blood to the body.\n4. Fe2+ and Fe3+ are different forms of iron. Fe2+ is the reduced form and Fe3+ is the oxidized form. Cyanosis can occur when there is an increase in the concentration of reduced hemoglobin in the blood, which can be caused by a decrease in the amount of oxygen available to bind to hemoglobin or an increase in the amount of reduced hemoglobin.\n5. Mitochondrial cytochrome c oxidase is an enzyme that is involved in the electron transport chain in mitochondria. Inhibition of this enzyme can lead to a decrease in the amount of oxygen available to bind to hemoglobin, which can cause cyanosis.\n6. Heme groups are iron-containing molecules that are part of hemoglobin. Allosteric alteration of heme groups can affect the ability of hemoglobin to bind to oxygen, which can cause cyanosis.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "603da89f-d091-4bb0-a8c6-3d79a7dc167c",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Inhibition of mitochondrial cytochrome c oxidase, as this can lead to a decrease in the amount of oxygen available to bind to hemoglobin, causing cyanosis.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
