                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Inhibition of mitochondrial cytochrome c oxidase. This enzyme is involved in the electron transport chain in mitochondria, which is essential for cellular respiration and energy production. Inhibition of cytochrome c oxidase can impair oxygen utilization and cause cyanosis. The inhaled medication that the newborn was started on may have inhibited this enzyme, leading to the initial improvement in tachypnea and oxygenation status, but then causing cyanosis three hours later.",
