                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nB) Failure of processus vaginalis to obliterate\n\nThis presentation is consistent with a hydrocele, which is caused by an accumulation of fluid within the tunica vaginalis, the sac that surrounds the testis. In adults, hydroceles are usually due to a failure of the processus vaginalis to obliterate, leading to persistent communication between the peritoneal cavity and the scrotum. This communication allows peritoneal fluid to accumulate in the scrotum, resulting in a painless, cystic, transilluminating mass. The other answer choices are not consistent with the clinical presentation.",
