                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What fetal cells are stimulated by the administration of a single dose of betamethasone in a 26-year-old gravida 2 para 1 at 24 weeks gestation with preterm labor?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- The patient is experiencing mild abdominal cramps, uterine contractions, and a watery vaginal discharge, which are signs of preterm labor.\n- The patient has a history of preterm birth, which increases the risk of preterm labor.\n- The pelvic examination reveals cervical softening and shortening, which are also signs of preterm labor.\n- The transvaginal ultrasound shows a cervical length of 12 mm, which is consistent with preterm labor.\n- A tocolytic and a single dose of betamethasone are administered to prevent preterm delivery.\n- Betamethasone is a corticosteroid that can stimulate fetal lung maturation and reduce the risk of respiratory distress syndrome in preterm infants.\n- Therefore, the fetal cells that are stimulated by betamethasone are likely to be lung cells.\n- Type I and Type II pneumocytes are the two main types of lung cells, and they are responsible for gas exchange and surfactant production, respectively.\n- Goblet cells and bronchial epithelial cells are also present in the lungs, but they are not directly involved in fetal lung maturation.\n- Vascular smooth myocytes are muscle cells that are found in blood vessels, and they are not related to fetal lung maturation.\n- Therefore, the correct answer is D) Type II pneumocytes.\n\nAnswer: D) Type II pneumocytes.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "68eab2e8-dab6-416a-b390-1ade8b68f417",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Type II pneumocytes.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "D",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
