                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient is a 65-year-old woman who has gone through menopause and has a family history of breast cancer. She has hypertension and a low bone mineral density score. The physician is considering treatment with raloxifene, which is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that can help prevent bone loss and reduce the risk of breast cancer.\n\nHowever, raloxifene has been associated with an increased risk of pulmonary embolism, which is a blood clot in the lungs. Therefore, option A is correct.\n\nCellulitis is a bacterial skin infection and is not related to raloxifene treatment, so option B is incorrect.\n\nRaloxifene has been shown to reduce the risk of breast cancer, so option C is incorrect.\n\nMandibular osteonecrosis is a rare but serious side effect of some medications used to treat osteoporosis, but it is not associated with raloxifene treatment, so option D is incorrect.\n\nHypercholesterolemia is not a known side effect of raloxifene, so option E is incorrect.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Pulmonary embolism.",
