                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify the medication raloxifene and its mechanism of action.\n2. Research the potential side effects of raloxifene.\n3. Determine which of the listed conditions is a potential side effect of raloxifene.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Raloxifene is a selective estrogen receptor modulator (SERM) that works by binding to estrogen receptors in certain tissues, such as bone and breast tissue, and blocking the effects of estrogen in other tissues, such as the uterus.\n2. According to the FDA, potential side effects of raloxifene include hot flashes, leg cramps, swelling of the hands/feet, flu-like symptoms, joint pain, and increased risk of blood clots, including deep vein thrombosis (DVT) and pulmonary embolism (PE). Other potential side effects include stroke, endometrial cancer, and cataracts.\n3. Based on the potential side effects listed, the correct answer is A) Pulmonary embolism. Raloxifene has been shown to increase the risk of blood clots, including PE, which can be life-threatening. While breast cancer is a concern for this patient given her family history, raloxifene is actually used to reduce the risk of breast cancer in certain women. Cellulitis, mandibular osteonecrosis, and hypercholesterolemia are not known side effects of raloxifene.",
