                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Coagulation is a complex process involving multiple factors and pathways. Platelets, clotting factors, and endothelial cells all play a role in the process. Bleeding disorders can be caused by defects in any of these components.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the normal values for platelet count, bleeding time, prothrombin time, activated partial thromboplastin time, factor VIII activity, and ristocetin cofactor assay?\n2. What is the significance of a decreased factor VIII activity and ristocetin cofactor assay?\n3. What are the functions of factors IX, Gp Ib, XI, vitamin K, and antithrombin III in coagulation?\n4. Which of these factors is most likely to be affected in a patient with bleeding gums?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Normal values for platelet count are typically between 150,000-450,000/mm3. Normal bleeding time is less than 9 minutes. Normal prothrombin time is 11-13 seconds. Normal activated partial thromboplastin time is 25-35 seconds. Normal factor VIII activity is 50-150%. Normal ristocetin cofactor assay is greater than 50%.\n2. Decreased factor VIII activity and ristocetin cofactor assay are indicative of a deficiency in von Willebrand factor, which is necessary for platelet adhesion and aggregation.\n3. Factor IX is involved in the intrinsic pathway of coagulation. Gp Ib is a receptor on platelets that binds von Willebrand factor. Factor XI is also involved in the intrinsic pathway. Vitamin K is necessary for the production of several clotting factors. Antithrombin III is a natural anticoagulant that inhibits thrombin and other clotting factors.\n4. Based on the lab values and symptoms described, a deficiency in von Willebrand factor is the most likely cause of the patient's bleeding gums. This would affect Gp Ib and factor VIII activity, which are both involved in platelet adhesion and aggregation. Therefore, the answer is B) Gp Ib.",
                        "answers": [
