                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is B) Clusters of bland cells without mitotic activity.\nA cardiac myxoma is a tumor of the heart. It is the most common primary tumor of the heart, and is found in the left atrium in about 75% of cases. It is attached to the interatrial septum by a stalk.\nA myxoma is a benign tumor composed of primitive connective tissue cells. It is a round or oval mass with a gelatinous consistency.\nThe tumor cells are bland spindle-shaped cells with a low mitotic rate. The tumor cells are positive for muscle-specific actin and desmin, but negative for myoglobin, myosin, and CD34.\nThe differential diagnosis includes lipoma, which is a benign fatty tumor, and rhabdomyoma, which is a tumor of striated muscle.\nThe correct answer is B) Clusters of bland cells without mitotic activity.",
