                    {
                        "id": "6a4efb82-5026-4c48-8ca7-9452acd1afde",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The patient is a 59-year-old man who has been hospitalized for 5 days for acute myocardial infarction. He now complains of chest pain that has been present for 4 hours, which is similar in nature to what initially brought him into the hospital. His vital signs are stable, but his ECG is difficult to interpret. Of the laboratory tests listed, an abnormal result of which would have the most diagnostic utility?\n\nThe most likely diagnosis for the patient's current symptoms is recurrent myocardial infarction. The laboratory test that would have the most diagnostic utility in this situation is Troponin T. Troponin T is a cardiac-specific biomarker that is released into the bloodstream when there is damage to the heart muscle. It is the preferred biomarker for the diagnosis of myocardial infarction and is more sensitive and specific than other biomarkers such as CK-MB.\n\nAlanine aminotransferase and alkaline phosphatase are liver enzymes and would not be useful in the diagnosis of myocardial infarction. Lactate dehydrogenase is a nonspecific biomarker that can be elevated in a variety of conditions, including myocardial infarction, but it is not as sensitive or specific as Troponin T. CK-MB is a cardiac-specific biomarker, but it is not as sensitive or specific as Troponin T and has largely been replaced by Troponin T in the diagnosis of myocardial infarction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is E) Troponin T.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "2cc48c19-a52b-409a-9f8d-77c3935f5637",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
