                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Hi professor, can you explain the case of the 59-year-old man with chest pain?\n\nProfessor: Sure, the man has been in the hospital for 5 days due to an acute myocardial infarction. He was treated with alteplase and has been under close observation. However, he is now experiencing chest pain and discomfort in his left shoulder, similar to what brought him to the hospital initially.\n\nStudent: What are his vital signs?\n\nProfessor: His pulse is 86/min, respiratory rate is 16/min, and blood pressure is 146/90 mm Hg.\n\nStudent: Did the doctor find anything abnormal during chest auscultation?\n\nProfessor: No, there were no abnormal findings.\n\nStudent: What about his ECG?\n\nProfessor: The ECG is difficult to interpret.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what laboratory test would be most useful in diagnosing the cause of his chest pain?\n\nProfessor: Of the options given, an abnormal result of Troponin T would have the most diagnostic utility. Troponin T is a protein that is released into the bloodstream when there is damage to the heart muscle, so an abnormal result would indicate that the patient is experiencing another myocardial infarction. \n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that, professor.",
