 include a shorter procedure time and lower risk of complications compared to other surgical methods. Risks include bleeding, infection, and the possibility of incomplete abortion.\n- Oral mifepristone + misoprostol: Benefits include a non-invasive method and the ability to have the abortion at home. Risks include bleeding, infection, and the possibility of incomplete abortion.\n\nAnswering sub-question 3:\n3. Based on the patient's age, previous vaginal deliveries, and desire for elective abortion, the most appropriate procedure would be Dilatation and evacuation (D&E). This procedure has a shorter",
