                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The ECG is a tool used to measure the electrical activity of the heart. It can help diagnose various heart conditions.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the ECG showing?\n2. What are the symptoms of hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy?\n3. What are the symptoms of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation?\n4. What is Brugada syndrome?\n5. What are the symptoms of ventricular tachycardia?\n6. What is sick sinus syndrome?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The ECG is not shown in the prompt, so we cannot answer this sub-question.\n2. Symptoms of hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy include shortness of breath, chest pain, fainting, and heart palpitations.\n3. Symptoms of paroxysmal atrial fibrillation include heart palpitations, shortness of breath, weakness, and fatigue.\n4. Brugada syndrome is a genetic condition that can cause abnormal heart rhythms and sudden cardiac death.\n5. Symptoms of ventricular tachycardia include rapid heartbeat, dizziness, fainting, and chest pain.\n6. Sick sinus syndrome is a condition where the heart's natural pacemaker does not function properly, causing an irregular heartbeat and symptoms such as dizziness, fatigue, and shortness of breath.\n\nAnswer: Based on the symptoms described in the prompt, the most likely diagnosis is B) Paroxysmal atrial fibrillation.",
