depressive disorder: This diagnosis requires the presence of a depressed mood for most of the day, more days than not, for at least 2 years. The patient's episodes of depressed mood seem to resolve after 4-6 weeks, which does not meet the criteria for this diagnosis. Therefore, this diagnosis is unlikely.\n- Schizoaffective disorder: This diagnosis requires the presence of both psychotic symptoms and mood symptoms that meet the criteria for a major depressive episode, manic episode, or mixed episode. There is no mention of psychotic symptoms in this case,",
