                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Decreased residual volume\n\nAs we age, our respiratory system undergoes several changes, including decreased lung elasticity, decreased chest wall compliance, and decreased respiratory muscle strength. These changes can lead to a decrease in lung volumes, including vital capacity and residual volume. In this patient, the fact that her respiratory rate is normal and there are no abnormalities on physical examination suggests that her respiratory function is likely well-preserved. Therefore, the most likely change in respiratory function compared to a healthy 20-year-old woman is a decrease in residual volume. This is because residual volume tends to increase with age due to decreased lung elasticity and airway closure. The other answer choices are less likely to be present in this patient based on the information provided.",
