                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient is socially isolated, feels lonely, and is extremely sensitive to criticism, even from family. She also believes that she is untalented and that nobody wants to hang out with her. When her mother encourages her to invite friends over, she bursts into tears and says that she will end up getting rejected. These symptoms are consistent with avoidant personality disorder (C). \n\nSchizotypal personality disorder (A) is characterized by odd beliefs, magical thinking, and eccentric behavior. Generalized anxiety disorder (B) is characterized by excessive worry and anxiety about a variety of events or activities. Paranoid personality disorder (D) is characterized by a pervasive distrust and suspiciousness of others. Dependent personality disorder (E) is characterized by a pervasive need to be taken care of and a fear of separation from others. None of these disorders fully capture the patient's symptoms.",
