                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) Mifepristone.\n\nExplanation:\n\nThe patient has confirmed her pregnancy and has decided to medically abort her 6-week pregnancy. Mifepristone is a medication used for medical abortion in the first trimester of pregnancy. It works by blocking the hormone progesterone, which is necessary for the pregnancy to continue. This causes the lining of the uterus to break down and the pregnancy to be terminated. Megestrol is a progestin medication used to treat breast cancer and appetite loss. Tamoxifen is a medication used to treat breast cancer. Terbutaline is a medication used to treat asthma and premature labor. The copper intrauterine device is a form of long-acting reversible contraception and is not used for medical abortion.",
