ible cause of the patient's symptoms.\n\nStudent: So which answer choice is the correct one?\n\nProfessor: Based on the symptoms described, the most likely answer is E) Gram-negative bacteria producing exotoxin that inactivates elongation factor 2. This is because the patient has a pseudomembrane in the throat, which is a common symptom of diphtheria, a bacterial infection caused by Corynebacterium diphtheriae. This bacteria produces a toxin that inactivates",
