ng cessation.\n\nE) This patient has no contraindications for bupropion and may safely use it.\n- This statement is incorrect. The patient has a history of seizure disorder, which is a relative contraindication for bupropion use. The medication can be considered with caution and close monitoring, but it is not completely safe for this patient.\n\nTherefore, the correct statement regarding the use of an antidepressant for smoking cessation in this patient is C) Bupropion lowers the seizure threshold and it should not be taken by patients with a",
