                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's differentiate using step by step reasoning like a medical expert:\n\nA type 1 error occurs when the null hypothesis is true but is rejected in error.\n\nThe null hypothesis is that mepolizumab has no effect on asthma exacerbations. So, if the null hypothesis is true, then mepolizumab would have no effect on asthma exacerbations.\n\nHowever, the study found that mepolizumab does reduce asthma exacerbations. So, if the null hypothesis is true, then the study would have found that mepolizumab does not reduce asthma exacerbations.\n\nTherefore, a type 1 error would occur if the null hypothesis is true but the study found that mepolizumab does reduce asthma exacerbations.",
                        "answers": [
