wever, the physical findings in this patient (e.g. white plaque-like lesions, atrophy of the labia minora) suggest a more localized vulvar condition.\n\nStep 3: Choose the most likely diagnosis based on the symptoms and findings.\nBased on the patient's symptoms and physical examination, the most likely diagnosis is B) Lichen sclerosus. This condition is characterized by chronic inflammation and scarring of",
