                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The given symptoms suggest a possible diagnosis of lichen planus, a chronic inflammatory skin condition.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is lichen planus?\n2. What are the clinical features of lichen planus?\n3. What are the microscopic findings in lichen planus?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Lichen planus is a chronic inflammatory skin condition that affects the skin, mucous membranes, hair, and nails.\n2. The clinical features of lichen planus include flat-topped, violaceous papules, itching, and thinning of nails with onycholysis.\n3. The microscopic finding observed in lichen planus is acantholysis, which is the separation of epidermal cells from each other due to damage to the intercellular connections.",
