                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what flat topped violaceous papules are?\n\nProfessor: Sure, flat topped means that the surface of the papules is flat rather than raised or rounded, and violaceous means that they have a bluish-purple color.\n\nStudent: What does thinning of nails mean?\n\nProfessor: Thinning of nails means that the nails are becoming thinner and weaker, which can cause them to break or split more easily.\n\nStudent: What is onycholysis?\n\nProfessor: Onycholysis is a condition where the nail separates from the nail bed, usually starting at the tip of the nail and working its way back towards the cuticle.\n\nStudent: So, what is the microscopic finding observed in this patient?\n\nProfessor: The correct answer is D) Acantholysis. Acantholysis is a condition where the cells in the outermost layer of the skin (the epidermis) separate from each other, causing the skin to become fragile and easily damaged. This is a characteristic finding in a condition called pemphigus vulgaris, which can present with the symptoms described in the question.",
