                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe question is asking which condition(s) do not require estimation of blood sugar. Let's analyze each option:\n\nA) Birth asphyxia: When a baby experiences birth asphyxia, their oxygen supply is compromised, which can lead to hypoglycemia (low blood sugar). Therefore, estimation of blood sugar is relevant in this condition. \n\nB) Large for date baby: A large for date baby (also known as macrosomia) is at risk for hypoglycemia due to the excess insulin production that occurs in response to high blood sugar levels. Therefore, estimation of blood sugar is relevant in this condition. \n\nC) Baby of hypothyroid mother: Hypothyroidism in the mother can lead to fetal hypoglycemia, so estimation of blood sugar is relevant in this condition. \n\nD) Rh Incompatibility: Rh incompatibility is a condition where the mother's blood type is Rh-negative and the baby's blood type is Rh-positive. This can lead to hemolytic disease of the newborn, which can cause anemia and jaundice, but it does not directly affect blood sugar levels. Therefore, estimation of blood sugar is not relevant in this condition. \n\nBased on the above analysis, the correct answer is D) Rh Incompatibility.",
