                        "cot": "\n\nD) Competition with PABA in folic acid synthesis. \n\nDapsone works by inhibiting the enzyme dihydropteroate synthase, which is involved in the synthesis of folic acid. By competing with para-aminobenzoic acid (PABA), a precursor of folic acid, dapsone prevents the formation of folic acid, which is essential for the growth and replication of bacteria and fungi. Additionally, dapsone has immunomodulatory effects by suppressing the activity of certain immune cells, such as neutrophils and eosinophils.",
