                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nDifficult. \n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\nThe question describes a patient with symptoms that suggest rabies after a dog bite. The corneal impression has been taken, and the question asks what test will be done on it for the most accurate diagnosis.\n\nOption A, indirect immunofluorescence, is a test that can detect antibodies against the rabies virus in a patient's blood. However, this test is not typically done on a corneal impression.\n\nOption B, PCR for virus, is a test that can detect the genetic material of the rabies virus in a patient's sample. This test can be done on a corneal impression and is a highly accurate way to diagnose rabies.\n\nOption C, histopathological examination for Negri bodies, involves looking for characteristic structures called Negri bodies in a patient's tissue sample. Negri bodies are found in the brain tissue of animals infected with rabies, but they are not always present in human cases of rabies. This test is not typically done on a corneal impression.\n\nOption D, antibodies against Rabies virus, is similar to option A in that it detects antibodies against the rabies virus in a patient's blood. This test is not typically done on a corneal impression.\n\nTherefore, the most accurate test to diagnose rabies from a corneal impression is option B, PCR for virus.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "58bc0bc6-c112-44b8-8691-02f7025f4f47",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) PCR for virus.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
