                        "cot": "\n1. The fertilized egg undergoes a series of cleavage divisions.\n2. The cells of the morula become arranged into a solid mass of cells called a blastocyst.\n3. The blastocyst has an inner cell mass and an outer layer called the trophoblast.\n4. The inner cell mass gives rise to the embryo.\n5. The trophoblast gives rise to extraembryonic structures.\n6. The extraembryonic structures include the placenta and the amniotic sac.\n7. The amniotic sac is filled with fluid and protects the embryo.\n8. The fluid-filled amniotic sac is called the amniotic cavity.\n9. The amniotic cavity is continuous with the cells of the yolk sac.\n10. The yolk sac provides nutrition to the embryo.\n11. The yolk sac is connected to the amniotic sac by a narrow stalk.\n12. The stalk is called the umbilical cord.\n\nThe correct answer is B) Ectoderm from epiblast; mesoderm and endoderm from hypoblast.",
