                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe epiblast and hypoblast are two layers of cells that form during early embryonic development. The epiblast is the upper layer, while the hypoblast is the lower layer. \n\nDuring gastrulation, the cells of the epiblast migrate and form three distinct layers: the ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm. The ectoderm gives rise to the skin, nervous system, and other tissues. The mesoderm gives rise to muscle, bone, and other tissues. The endoderm gives rise to the lining of the digestive and respiratory systems.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Ectoderm and mesoderm from epiblast; endoderm from hypoblast.",
