                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) Ectoderm and mesoderm are derived from the epiblast, while endoderm is derived from the hypoblast.\n\nExplanation:\nDuring embryonic development, the blastocyst (a hollow ball of cells) implants into the uterine wall and begins to differentiate into different cell types. The inner cell mass of the blastocyst gives rise to the epiblast and hypoblast layers.\n\nThe epiblast layer gives rise to the ectoderm and mesoderm germ layers, which form the outer and middle layers of the embryo, respectively. The ectoderm gives rise to the skin, nervous system, and other structures, while the mesoderm gives rise to the muscles, bones, and other organs.\n\nThe hypoblast layer gives rise to the endoderm germ layer, which forms the innermost layer of the embryo and gives rise to the lining of the digestive and respiratory tracts, as well as other internal organs.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Ectoderm and mesoderm are derived from the epiblast, while endoderm is derived from the hypoblast.",
