                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Where do the three embryonic germ layers (ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm) come from?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- The embryonic germ layers are the three primary layers of cells that form during embryonic development.\n- The epiblast and hypoblast are two layers of cells that form the early embryo.\n- Therefore, the question is asking which of these two layers gives rise to the three germ layers.\n\nAnswer: C) Ectoderm and mesoderm come from the epiblast, while endoderm comes from the hypoblast.",
