                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: What are the embryonic germ layers?\nThe embryonic germ layers are the three primary layers of cells that form during embryonic development. These layers give rise to all the tissues and organs of the body.\n\nStep 2: What is the epiblast and hypoblast?\nThe epiblast and hypoblast are two layers of cells that form during early embryonic development. The epiblast gives rise to the embryo proper, while the hypoblast forms the yolk sac.\n\nStep 3: Which layer(s) give rise to the three embryonic germ layers?\nAccording to the question, we need to determine which layer(s) give rise to the ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm. \n\nOption A) Epiblast only - This option suggests that all three germ layers are derived from the epiblast alone. However, this is not correct as the hypoblast also plays a role in germ layer formation.\n\nOption B) Ectoderm from epiblast; mesoderm and endoderm from hypoblast - This option suggests that the ectoderm is derived from the epiblast, while the mesoderm and endoderm are derived from the hypoblast. This is not correct as the mesoderm and endoderm are actually derived from the epiblast.\n\nOption C) Ectoderm and mesoderm from epiblast; endoderm from hypoblast - This option suggests that the ectoderm and mesoderm are derived from the epiblast, while the endoderm is derived from the hypoblast. This is the correct answer as it accurately reflects the origin of the three germ layers.\n\nOption D) Hypoblast only - This option suggests that all three germ layers are derived from the hypoblast alone. However, this is not correct as the epiblast also plays a role in germ layer formation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Ectoderm and mesoderm from epiblast; endoderm from hypoblast.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "3440fd8c-e17d-45a7-baa8-e4171f60388c",
