                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Identify the possible causes of high grade fever, inspiratory stridor, and swallowing difficulty with drooling of saliva.\n2. Determine which of the possible causes require treatment beyond general airway management.\n3. Evaluate the options for treatment beyond general airway management.\n4. Choose the recommended treatment based on the evaluation.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. Possible causes of high grade fever, inspiratory stridor, and swallowing difficulty with drooling of saliva include epiglottitis, croup, and bacterial tracheitis.\n2. Epiglottitis and bacterial tracheitis require treatment beyond general airway management, while croup can often be managed with general airway management.\n3. The options for treatment beyond general airway management include nebulized racemic epinephrine, anti-diphtheria toxin, corticosteroids, and IV ceftriaxone.\n4. The recommended treatment for epiglottitis and bacterial tracheitis is IV ceftriaxone and corticosteroids. Therefore, the correct answer is C) Corticosteroids.",
