                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Nebulized racemic epinephrine is a treatment option for croup, which presents with inspiratory stridor and can cause difficulty swallowing and drooling. Therefore, this option is a possible correct answer.\n\nB) Anti-diphtheria toxin is not a recommended treatment for croup. This option is not correct.\n\nC) Corticosteroids are a recommended treatment for croup and can help reduce inflammation in the airways. Therefore, this option is a possible correct answer.\n\nD) IV ceftriaxone is an antibiotic and is not a recommended treatment for croup. This option is not correct.\n\nCombining all the information, options A and C are possible correct answers for the treatment of croup. Therefore, the correct answer is either A or C.\n\nMapping the answer to one of the multiple choice answers, the closest option is C) Corticosteroids. Therefore, the answer is C) Corticosteroids.",
