                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What are the possible side effects of a 12mg mistakenly dose of epidural morphine in a patient with biliary duct stricture, retching, and vomiting who is already receiving 3mg morphine epidurally daily?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Biliary duct stricture is a condition where the bile ducts become narrow, which can cause pain, nausea, and vomiting.\n- Retching is a type of vomiting where the patient makes repeated attempts to vomit but nothing comes out.\n- Morphine is a strong painkiller that can also cause side effects such as itching, urinary retention, nausea, and respiratory depression.\n- Epidural administration of morphine means that the drug is injected into the space around the spinal cord, which can provide pain relief without affecting the whole body.\n- The patient is already receiving 3mg of morphine epidurally daily, which suggests that they have significant pain that requires strong pain management.\n- However, a 12mg mistakenly dose of epidural morphine is a significant increase in the amount of the drug that the patient is receiving, which can lead to more side effects.\n\nTherefore, the possible side effects of a 12mg mistakenly dose of epidural morphine in this patient may include:\n\nA) Itching - Morphine can cause itching as a side effect, but it is not necessarily related to the dose.\nB) Urinary retention - Morphine can cause urinary retention by relaxing the muscles that control urination, but it is not necessarily related to the dose.\nC) Increase vomiting - Morphine can cause nausea and vomiting as a side effect, and a higher dose can increase the likelihood of this side effect.\nD) Overstimulation of respiratory centre - Morphine can depress the respiratory centre in the brainstem, which can lead to breathing difficulties or even respiratory arrest. A higher dose can increase the risk of this side effect.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Overstimulation of respiratory centre.",
