                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Natural disasters can cause significant damage to property and loss of life. Different types of natural disasters have varying impacts on human life.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a hydrological disaster?\n2. What is a meteorological disaster?\n3. What is a geological disaster?\n4. What is a fire disaster?\n5. Which type of natural disaster has caused the maximum deaths in history?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A hydrological disaster is a natural disaster caused by water, such as floods, tsunamis, and landslides.\n2. A meteorological disaster is a natural disaster caused by weather, such as hurricanes, tornadoes, and blizzards.\n3. A geological disaster is a natural disaster caused by the Earth's crust, such as earthquakes, volcanic eruptions, and avalanches.\n4. A fire disaster is a natural disaster caused by fire, such as wildfires and bushfires.\n5. According to historical data, the type of natural disaster that has caused the maximum deaths is a geological disaster, specifically earthquakes. The deadliest earthquake in history occurred in China in 1556, killing an estimated 830,000 people.",
