                        "cot": "\n\n1. Systematic random sampling: This method involves selecting every nth patient from a list of patients. It does not take into account any potential factors that may affect the results, so it is not the correct answer.\n\n2. Simple random sampling: This method involves randomly selecting patients from a list of patients. While it is a valid method, it does not take into account any potential factors that may affect the results, so it is not the correct answer.\n\n3. Stratified random sampling: This method involves dividing patients into subgroups based on potential factors that may affect the results, and then randomly selecting patients from each subgroup. This is the correct answer, as it takes into account potential factors that may affect the results.\n\n4. Cluster sampling: This method involves selecting groups of patients (clusters) rather than individual patients. It may be useful in certain situations, but it does not take into account potential factors that may affect the results, so it is not the correct answer.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Stratified random sampling.",
