                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about what each of these drugs does. \n\nMetoprolol is a beta blocker. Beta blockers work by blocking the beta receptors on cells, which slows down the heart rate. \n\nVerapamil is a calcium channel blocker. Calcium channel blockers work by blocking the calcium channels on cells, which decreases the force of contraction of the heart. \n\nThe combination of these two drugs will result in bradycardia with AV block.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
