                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what ptosis is?\n\nProfessor: Ptosis is a drooping of the upper eyelid. It can be caused by a variety of factors, including muscle weakness or nerve damage.\n\nStudent: What is the finger abduction test?\n\nProfessor: The finger abduction test is a way to assess extraocular muscle movement. It involves asking the patient to hold their fingers outstretched and then moving them in different directions while observing the eyes.\n\nStudent: What is a myopathic pattern on an ERG?\n\nProfessor: A myopathic pattern on an ERG indicates that there is a problem with the muscle itself, rather than the nerves that control it.\n\nStudent: Can you explain what a decremental response in orbicularis means?\n\nProfessor: A decremental response in orbicularis means that there is a decrease in the strength of the muscle contraction with repeated stimulation. This is a characteristic finding in myasthenia gravis.\n\nStudent: So, based on the information provided, what is the most probable diagnosis?\n\nProfessor: Based on the symptoms and test results, the most probable diagnosis would be A) Ocular myasthenia gravis.",
