                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) Roth spot: This is a feature of infective endocarditis, where there is a white spot with a red halo seen in the retina of the eye.\n\nB) Osler's nodes: These are painful nodules seen on the fingers and toes, which are a feature of infective endocarditis.\n\nC) Aschoff nodules: These are not a feature of infective endocarditis. They are seen in rheumatic fever, which is a different condition.\n\nD) Positive blood culture: This is a feature of infective endocarditis, where the blood culture shows the presence of bacteria.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) Aschoff nodules.",
