                    {
                        "id": "cdf5844c-927f-40a2-bbd1-428928dccb35",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the concept of infective endocarditis.\nInfective endocarditis is an infection of the inner lining of the heart chambers and heart valves. It is caused by bacteria, fungi, or other microorganisms that enter the bloodstream and attach to damaged areas of the heart. The infection can cause a range of symptoms, including fever, fatigue, joint pain, and heart murmurs.\n\nStep 2: Understand the features of infective endocarditis.\nThere are several features of infective endocarditis that can be used to diagnose the condition. These include:\n\n- Roth spots: These are small, white spots that appear on the retina of the eye. They are caused by small clots that form as a result of the infection.\n- Osler's nodes: These are painful, red or purple bumps that appear on the fingers and toes. They are caused by inflammation of the blood vessels.\n- Aschoff nodules: These are small, painless nodules that appear on the heart valves. They are caused by inflammation of the heart tissue.\n- Positive blood culture: This is a test that is used to detect the presence of bacteria or other microorganisms in the bloodstream. A positive blood culture is a strong indicator of infective endocarditis.\n\nStep 3: Identify the feature that is not a feature of infective endocarditis.\nBased on the features listed above, we can see that all of the options except for C) Aschoff nodules are features of infective endocarditis. Aschoff nodules are actually a feature of rheumatic fever, which is a different condition that can also affect the heart.\n\nStep 4: Answer the question.\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"Which of the following is not a feature of infective endocarditis?\" is C) Aschoff nodules.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "65eb588a-0cb5-414f-808b-db3b06b1d9a9",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Aschoff nodules.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
