                        "cot": "\n\nWhen we talk about lateral movement of the condyle, we are referring to the movement of the mandible to the side. This movement is achieved by the contraction of the lateral pterygoid muscle on the same side as the direction of movement. Therefore, the correct answer is B) Ipsilateral lateral pterygoid. The contralateral lateral pterygoid and same side medial pterygoid do not play a significant role in lateral movement of the condyle.",
