                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Identify what is meant by \"lateral movement of condyle.\"\n2. Determine which muscles are involved in lateral movement of the condyle.\n3. Evaluate each answer choice to see if it matches the muscles involved in lateral movement of the condyle.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. Lateral movement of condyle refers to the movement of the mandibular condyle (part of the jaw bone) away from the midline of the skull.\n2. The lateral pterygoid muscles are responsible for lateral movement of the condyle.\n3. \nA) Contralateral lateral pterygoid - This answer choice is incorrect because the contralateral (opposite side) lateral pterygoid muscle would not be involved in lateral movement of the condyle.\nB) Ispilateral lateral pterygoid - This answer choice is correct because the ipsilateral (same side) lateral pterygoid muscle is responsible for lateral movement of the condyle.\nC) Same side medial pterygoid - This answer choice is incorrect because the medial pterygoid muscle is responsible for elevating the mandible, not for lateral movement of the condyle.\nD) None of the above - This answer choice is incorrect because answer choice B is correct. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Ispilateral lateral pterygoid.",
