                    {
                        "id": "7761cc1f-830e-4469-9dcc-4c2fa6936a60",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the HDI calculation\nThe Human Development Index (HDI) is a composite index that measures a country's average achievements in three dimensions of human development: a long and healthy life, access to knowledge, and a decent standard of living. The HDI is calculated by taking into account three indicators: life expectancy at birth, gross enrolment ratio, and gross national income per capita. \n\nStep 2: Analyze the statements\nA) In gross enrolment, only secondary education is considered, not primary education - This statement is true. The gross enrolment ratio is calculated as the number of students enrolled in primary, secondary, and tertiary education, regardless of age, divided by the population of the age group that officially corresponds to the level of education. However, for the purpose of HDI calculation, only the secondary education enrolment ratio is considered. \n\nB) 1/3rd weightage is given to adult literacy - This statement is true. Adult literacy rate is one of the indicators used to measure access to knowledge, and it is given a weightage of 1/3 in the HDI calculation. \n\nC) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolment - This statement is false. Gross enrolment ratio is given a weightage of 1/3 in the HDI calculation, not 2/3. \n\nD) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy - This statement is partially true. Adult literacy rate is one of the indicators used to measure access to knowledge, but it is not the only indicator. The HDI also takes into account the gross enrolment ratio, which reflects the level of education attainment in a country. \n\nStep 3: Identify the incorrect statement\nBased on the analysis, the incorrect statement is C) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolment. The correct weightage given to gross enrolment ratio is 1/3. Therefore, the answer is C.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "959235b8-94bb-4d88-ab82-a3b5d095da4f",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) 2/3`dweightage is given to gross enrolment.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
