                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Which of the following statements regarding the calculation of HDI is false?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- The HDI is a measure of human development that takes into account three dimensions: health (measured by life expectancy at birth), education (measured by years of schooling), and standard of living (measured by gross national income per capita).\n- A) This statement is true. The HDI only considers secondary education in the calculation of the education dimension, not primary education.\n- B) This statement is true. Adult literacy is one of the indicators used to measure the education dimension, and it is given a weight of 1/3 in the calculation of the dimension.\n- C) This statement is true. Gross enrolment is another indicator used to measure the education dimension, and it is given a weight of 2/3 in the calculation of the dimension.\n- D) This statement is false. The country's achievement in the education dimension is not computed solely on the basis of adult literacy, but on the basis of both adult literacy and gross enrolment.\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) Country's achievement is computed on the basis of adult literacy.",
