                    {
                        "id": "ce68427e-7c2b-45b4-a084-8363f4704255",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-09",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe child has low serum glucose, ketoacidosis, and decreased pH, which suggests a problem with glucose metabolism. Intravenous glucagon raises blood glucose levels after meals, but not after an overnight fast, which suggests a problem with glycogen metabolism. The liver biopsy shows increased glycogen in the liver, which further supports a glycogen storage disorder. \n\nBased on these findings, the enzyme likely to be defective in this child is glucose-6-phosphatase (option A). Glucose-6-phosphatase is responsible for converting glucose-6-phosphate to glucose, which is necessary for maintaining normal blood glucose levels during fasting. A deficiency in this enzyme leads to impaired glucose release from the liver, resulting in hypoglycemia and glycogen accumulation in the liver. This condition is known as glycogen storage disease type I (GSD-I) or von Gierke disease. \n\nMuscle phosphorylase (option B) is responsible for breaking down glycogen in muscle tissue, and a deficiency in this enzyme leads to glycogen accumulation in muscle tissue, resulting in muscle weakness. This condition is known as McArdle disease. However, the clinical presentation and liver biopsy findings in this case do not support a diagnosis of McArdle disease. \n\nBranching enzyme (option C) and debranching enzyme (option D) are involved in glycogen synthesis and breakdown, respectively. Deficiencies in these enzymes can lead to different types of glycogen storage diseases, but the clinical presentation and liver biopsy findings in this case do not support a diagnosis of either of these conditions.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f14aaf38-fc15-4a36-94ef-d4d44772c236",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) Glucose-6-phosphatase.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/16 19:33:13",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
