                        "cot": "\n\nA) High speed film: This option is incorrect because high speed film actually increases patient radiation. This is because it requires less exposure time, but the radiation intensity is higher.\n\nB) Intensifying screens: This option is correct. Intensifying screens are used to reduce patient radiation by decreasing the amount of radiation needed to produce an image. They work by converting X-rays into visible light, which exposes the film.\n\nC) Lead apron: This option is also correct. Lead aprons are used to shield the patient's body from unnecessary radiation exposure during radiographic procedures.\n\nD) Decreasing kVp: This option is incorrect. Decreasing kVp can actually increase patient radiation because it requires a longer exposure time to produce an image.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Intensifying screens.",
